        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nIt was because 'mini.base16' essentially used `vim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniTablineFill', {})`. This lead to clearing `MiniTablineFill` highlight group, which usually means that it is \"invisible\". But then during `require('mini.tabline').setup()` actual links are created and they do not agree with 'mini.base16'. **Edit**: Instead I think the main goal of 'mini.base16' was to indeed link to `Normal` but it didn't for some reason.\n\nI've updated 'mini.base16' (and 'mini.hues') to never use `{}` for plugin highlight groups to avoid situation from this issue. Should now be fixed on latest `main`.",
